      "message": "refactor(sim): a carried field bakes the turn's signed permutation into its bricks\n\nSdfField::turned(&LatticeTurn) -> (SdfField, Point3) re-indexes every layer\n(band bricks, cuts, cut_ups, the new cut_downs) brick by brick: brick b ->\n!b on a negated axis with its slot mirrored, axes swapped on a quarter turn.\nShell facets and the closed-form box are negated/swapped exactly. Only the\ntranslation is left as the view. On a flip, cut_ups and cut_downs trade\nplaces, and the field marks itself bounded_cuts so the E1 floor law refuses\nby name until E2b reads cut_downs. The cost ledger is re-keyed and every cut\nbrick is marked dirty.\n\nfield.rs's input gate moved to field_shell.rs (400-line law). Nothing calls\nturned yet (E2b, E2c).\n\nPinned bit-identical to the view for all 8 turns:\nfield_carry::a_baked_turn_reads_bit_for_bit_what_the_view_reads,\ncarry_engine_agreement::a_baked_turn_reads_what_the_view_reads_through_every_turn,\nand field_turn's unit tests.\n\nFixes #779\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
